+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository support
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add an `OrderRepository` method that writes `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents` and `coupon_code` for an order and returns the updated order; verify in `tests/coupon-application.test.ts` by applying values to an order inserted via `createApp` and reading them back.
+- [x] 1.2 Add a `CouponRepository` method that inserts a `coupon_redemptions` row and increments the coupon's `used_count`; verify with a test asserting `GET /coupons/:code` reports `usedCount` incremented and that a redemption row exists for the order.
+
+## 2. Apply-coupon service
+
+- [x] 2.1 Wire the existing `CouponRepository` instance into `OrderService` in `app.ts` (constructor change); verify `npm run build` type-checks.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` happy path with fixed and percentage discount math and the max-discount/amount caps; verify tests for `FIXED` 500 on 12000 → 11500, `PERCENT` 20 on 12000 → 9600, floor rounding (10% of 999 → 99), max cap, and discount clamped to the order amount.
+- [x] 2.3 Add order eligibility checks (exists, `PENDING`, no coupon yet) to `applyCoupon`; verify tests return `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` 404, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING` 409 and `ORDER_ALREADY_HAS_COUPON` 409 leaving the order unchanged.
+- [x] 2.4 Add coupon eligibility checks (exists, `ACTIVE`, validity window inclusive of `validFrom`/`validUntil`, `minAmountCents`, `usageLimit`) using `this.clock()`; verify tests return `COUPON_NOT_FOUND` 404, `COUPON_INACTIVE` 409, `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID` 409, `COUPON_EXPIRED` 409, `ORDER_BELOW_MIN_AMOUNT` 409 and `COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED` 409.
+- [x] 2.5 Record the redemption and increment `used_count` on successful application; verify the used-count test from 1.2 passes through the service path.
+
+## 3. HTTP route and integration
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `routes/orders.ts` mapping to `applyCoupon` with `parseId`, and reject a missing/non-string `couponCode` with `INVALID_REQUEST` 400; verify an end-to-end `app.request` test returns the updated order, and that a missing coupon code is a 400.
+- [x] 3.2 Run `npm test` and `npm run build` and verify all tests (including the pre-existing `tests/orders.test.ts`) and the type check pass.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change with `/opsx:archive` once review requirements are satisfied.
